<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: Czech builder IPS H1 gross rises.</title>
<headline>Czech builder IPS H1 gross rises.</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1997-07-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Czech construction group IPS Praha a.s. said on Monday that its first half consolidated pre-tax profit rose to 145.8 million crowns from a 106.1 million crown gross profit for the same period last year.</p>
<p>Total consolidated turnover rose to 6.324 billion crowns from 4.732 billion, according to Czech accounting standards, the firm said in a statement.  </p>
<p>consolidated</p>
<p> pre-tax profit (czk million)  145.800  vs    106.100</p>
<p> turnover		    6,324.000	4,732.000</p>
<p> employees			 5,881	    6,162</p>
<p>parent unconsolidated</p>
<p>  pre-tax profit	     115.389  vs    104.755</p>
<p>  operating profit	   151.582  vs    132.221</p>
<p>  writeoffs		     95.571  vs     79.491</p>
<p>  sales/own goods/serv.   3,837.474 vs  2,086.103</p>
<p>  sales of external goods   376.844 vs    300.767</p>
<p>  basic capital	     1,437.038 vs  1,437.038</p>
<p>  assets			9,453.336 vs  8,375.331</p>
<p>Note. The company said in the statement that it has forecast full-year 1997 gross profit to rise 36.4 percent year-on-year to 401 million crowns on sales of 11.647 billion crowns.</p>
<p>-- Prague Newsroom, 420-2-2423-0003</p>
</text>
